From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 15:57:05 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 137/139] drm/msm/dp: Don't redo the plug handling for a sink
 that is set up

Every "connected" notification runs the whole plug sequence: DPCD and
LTTPR caps, a full EDID read over AUX, the sink's D0 write and a reset
of the drive levels. With a DP alt-mode sink these notifications are
frequent while nothing changes: each Type-C HPD event is followed by the
compositor's forced probe, which calls .hpd_notify() again, and the
firmware repeats HPD a few seconds after the sink comes up. On a Lenovo
TB323FU with a 5120x2160 USB-C monitor each replug read the caps and
EDID five times, about 160 ms of AUX traffic each.

Remember when the caps and EDID of the current sink have been read and
skip the plug handling until it is unplugged, detect() loses it, or the
link was lost while streaming. A replug (ISR_HPD_REPLUG_COUNT) goes
through the unplug handler first, and IRQ_HPD is handled separately, so
real changes still get processed. A failed EDID read is retried on the
next notification.

Signed-off-by: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
index e20c381f1..fc3f97aa8 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
@@ -55,6 +55,7 @@ struct msm_dp_display_private {
 
 	struct mutex plugged_lock;
 	bool plugged;
+	bool sink_configured;
 	/* unplugged while the stream was on: retrain on the next plug */
 	bool link_lost;
 
@@ -278,6 +279,8 @@ static int msm_dp_display_process_hpd_high(struct msm_dp_display_private *dp)
 	u8 dpcd[DP_RECEIVER_CAP_SIZE];
 	const struct drm_edid *drm_edid = NULL;
 
+	dp->sink_configured = false;
+
 	rc = drm_dp_read_dpcd_caps(dp->aux, dpcd);
 	if (rc)
 		goto end;
@@ -319,6 +322,8 @@ static int msm_dp_display_process_hpd_high(struct msm_dp_display_private *dp)
 
 	msm_dp_link_reset_phy_params_vx_px(dp->link);
 
+	dp->sink_configured = drm_edid;
+
 end:
 	drm_edid_free(drm_edid);
 	return rc;
@@ -419,6 +424,9 @@ static int msm_dp_hpd_plug_handle(struct msm_dp_display_private *dp)
 
 	guard(mutex)(&dp->plugged_lock);
 
+	if (dp->plugged && dp->sink_configured && !dp->link_lost)
+		return 0;
+
 	/*
 	 * The plugged state holds one runtime PM reference, dropped by the
 	 * unplug handler. The Type-C side repeats "connected" notifications,
@@ -520,6 +528,7 @@ static int msm_dp_hpd_unplug_handle(struct msm_dp_display_private *dp)
 		pm_runtime_put_sync(&pdev->dev);
 		dp->plugged = false;
 	}
+	dp->sink_configured = false;
 
 	return 0;
 }
@@ -984,6 +993,7 @@ enum drm_connector_status msm_dp_bridge_detect(struct drm_bridge *bridge,
 	 * lose the state.
 	 */
 	if (!priv->plugged) {
+		priv->sink_configured = false;
 		if (phy_deinit) {
 			msm_dp_aux_enable_xfers(priv->aux, false);
 			msm_dp_display_host_phy_exit(priv);
-- 
